E AX3049 1120-arena-mark-into.ax:4:6-14 restriction-violated "`snapshot` claims `restrict(no-unsafe)` and the body performs Unsafe: snapshot -> __axiom_arena_mark_into" ^-:"__axiom_arena_mark_into" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-unsafe`, `no-foreign`, `no-cast:deep` and `no-recursion` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, or around the cycle, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3073 1120-arena-mark-into.ax:5:4-27 undeclared-unsafe "`snapshot` touches raw memory and its declaration does not say so" #"__axiom_arena_mark_into" ?4:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
